<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b990b9b0ff82cab05e56c9dcbe782d003acbedead5523505ca75d3339c73498</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Spy chief warns Russia conflict risk growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3046c879983666fc7abe32b48224208f11c59e4cd85f7d71fcb3d7eb0d4f0ab0</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789--3bde17a9e96c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is already waging a "shadow war" against Europe, the head of Germany's foreign intelligence service says. The Left Party is taking a case over remarks by the CDU's Katherina Reiche to a top court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz visits Kyiv as Russia strikes bridge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c19a5c2824a2a6dd011ec84e776e7c2e7c8851f866999704f2feec96058b5bd</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T14:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-strikes-bridge/a-79534734--9ac3ff548705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-strikes-bridge/a-79534734?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As air raid sirens sounded in Kyiv, Chancellor Merz called on President Putin to end his "senseless war" and announced new measures to support Ukraine, including plans for joint Ukrainian-German drone production.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Many believe Merkel more capable than Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2d687f655a34a034afb0d4f304180c0a58b9dc62d91f71e64dc6dbb24e614c0</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-many-believe-merkel-more-capable-than-merz/live-79528092--f23ed5eb8e52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-many-believe-merkel-more-capable-than-merz/live-79528092?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly half of Germans view former Chancellor Angela Merkel as better suited to handle Germany's challenges than current Chancellor Friedrich Merz. Also, today is the last day of Oktoberfest in Munich. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trust in the German Constitutional Court is eroding — how can this be stopped?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5b6b18ae084bbecb2143e531ba07a5e1d837e3ef368ebb4a81f3564fc709474</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211--cc048545c82f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's top court, which turned 75 this year, is losing the population's trust, surveys show. Some say reforms in the way it picks candidates would help, to also accept candidates nominated by the far-right AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German soccer: Can new coach Klopp turn things around?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d4b68a851fa90b5c4fb3af88eb03f8b0c433d4e89310914f487f96873e98ce7</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-soccer-can-new-coach-klopp-turn-things-around/a-79547308--04a0262a4a50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-soccer-can-new-coach-klopp-turn-things-around/a-79547308?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp has done things a little differently since becoming Germany coach. Casting a wider net for talent and trying to connect with players and country haven't made an immediate impact, but he is not bowed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
